<description>
Complete every magenta-marked transformed copy of the yellow/magenta template by painting the missing yellow cells.

Input structure
- The existing yellow pixels all lie inside one small rectangular template region.
- That template region is fully tiled by yellow and magenta pixels.
- Elsewhere, magenta pixels mark incomplete rotated or reflected copies of the same two-color template.

Rule
- Extract the template from the bounding box of all yellow pixels.
- For every rotated or reflected template placement whose magenta cells are all visible magenta pixels, paint each visible non-magenta yellow-template cell yellow.
- Allow yellow-template cells to be clipped off the grid edge, but require every magenta-template cell to be inside the grid.

Key insight
- The magenta cells are the alignment signature for each oriented copy; the yellow part of the same template is what must be restored.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "yellow/magenta rectangular template sprite s, including all rotated/reflected variants",
  "dst": "candidate grid placement d anchored by magenta pixels",
  "match_cond": "s.magenta mask is entirely in-bounds and equals magenta pixels at d; s.yellow cells may be clipped by the grid edge but cannot cover magenta",
  "transform": "paint every visible cell of the matched s.yellow mask yellow; keep all other cells unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16-19 rows x 12-17 cols
  background: random noise of colors {black, blue, azure} filling all non-template/non-pink cells
  template:
    size: 3x3 always
    colors: exactly yellow(4) and magenta(6), fully tiled (no other colors)
    yellow_cells: 4-6 of 9; pink_cells: 3-5 of 9
    asymmetry: no LR/UD/R90/R180 symmetry required, but may have anti-diagonal symmetry [observed]
    dihedral_variants: 4-8 distinct orientations depending on template symmetry
  complete_template: one copy with both yellow and pink cells visible, placed away from edges
  incomplete_copies:
    count: 1-3 rotated/reflected variants with pink cells present but yellow cells replaced by background
    each copy's pink cells match exactly one dihedral variant's pink mask
    yellow cells of the copy are absent (covered by background noise); solver restores them
    may be edge-clipped (yellow cells off-grid are allowed if all pink cells are in-bounds)
  distractor_pink: 13-22 additional magenta cells scattered across grid as singles or small clusters (1-4 cells)
  pink_density: ~10-13% of total grid cells are magenta
  output: same grid with each incomplete copy's missing yellow cells painted yellow; all else unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H x W in range. Fill entire grid with random {0,1,8} noise.
    2. Generate a random 3x3 template of yellow(4) and magenta(6) with 3-5 pink cells and 4-6 yellow cells; ensure no dihedral self-symmetry collapses variants below 4.
    3. Place the complete template (both colors) at a random interior position (not touching edges).
    4. Compute all dihedral variants. Choose 1-3 incomplete copies, each a (possibly distinct) variant.
    5. For each copy, pick a placement where all pink cells are in-bounds; yellow cells may be clipped at edges. Stamp pink cells onto grid. Record yellow cell positions as the expected output additions. Reject if any pink cell overlaps existing yellow/pink, or any in-bounds yellow cell overlaps existing pink.
    6. Scatter 13-22 distractor magenta cells on remaining background cells. Verify no distractor placement accidentally creates a new valid template match (re-run solver match logic; reject if spurious matches appear).
    7. Input = grid with distractors + copy pink cells but WITHOUT copy yellow cells. Output = grid with copy yellow cells painted in.
```
</generation_spec>
